      "message": "I\u0027m not following this description.  I see that `find_node_with_extra_flag()` calls `charge_get_flags()`, but doesn\u0027t use `get_chg_ctrl_mode()`.  Also, what does `CHARGE_CONTROL_NORMAL` mean?  Is the battery actively charging in this state?  `CHARGE_CONTROL_IDLE` appears to mean the battery is discharging (charging is idle).\n\nI wonder if these enums should all reference the battery state:\n```\nLED_BATT_IS_DISCHARGING  /* was LED_CHFLAG_FORCE_IDLE */\nLED_BATT_IS_CHARGING  /* was LED_CHFLAG_DEFAULT */\nLED_BATT_BELOW_10_PCT\nLED_BATT_ABOVE_10_PCT\n```\n\nWDYT?",
