      "writtenOn": "2022-06-05T00:40:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "charge_get_flags() implemented in [1] calls get_chg_ctrl_mode(). CHARGE_FLAG_FORCE_IDLE is set if charge_ctrl_mode !\u003d CHARGE_CONTROL_NORMAL and indicates factory mode during PWR_STATE_IDLE [2]. I don\u0027t understand the comment in [2] which states external power connected.\n\n[1] https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/charge_state_v2.c;l\u003d2230\n\n[2] https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/board/lazor/led.c;l\u003d109\n\nLED_BATT_BELOW_10_PCT and LED_BATT_ABOVE_10_PCT are removed, instead we are now using battery range in the batt-lvl property.",
